so  the next piece of the seven hours of  missing call logs story  is the obviously unbelievable claim from  donald trump that he doesn't even know  what burner phones are  so as a reminder yesterday we reported  to you  white house records turned over to the  january 6th committee are missing about  seven and a half hours of logs this is a  key seven and a half hours while the  insurrection was going on and one of the  sort of notable things  that came out of this was that donald  trump denied  having any idea what a burner phone is  in a statement monday night trump said i  have no idea what a burner phone is to  the best of my knowledge i have never  even heard the term  this stunk to high heaven and when i  told you this yesterday the story we  didn't know about john bolton's recent  comments  it was not plausible that trump didn't  know the term burner phone  and it was certainly not plausible that  trump doesn't know  about disposable phones  if you wanted to be as charitable as  possible and give trump the benefit of  the doubt which i don't know why we  would do at this point but let's say we  did you might be able to argue trump  knows of them as disposable phones  and he doesn't know or remember the term  burner phone but that it wasn't even  believable it really wasn't  we now have new reporting from donald  trump's former national security adviser  who says he specifically remembers trump  using the term burner phones and of  course this is completely believable and  completely obvious and it's what we  suspected right away  cbs news reporting john bolton the  former national security adviser to  trump told cbs news he heard trump use  the phrase burner phones in several  discussions and that trump did know  exactly what it meant  in a response trump said he never heard  the phrase burner phone i have no idea  what a burner phone is to the best of my  knowledge i've never even heard the term  bolton says he and trump spoke about how  people have used burner phones to avoid  having their calls scrutinized  um i mean  you know  i know trump's not the brightest  but it did not pass the sniff test that  trump didn't know what a burner phone  was  and this is increasingly reeking of  watergate i would encourage everybody in  the audience who is disturbed by this  story as you should be and you want to  read a little bit more about it there's  a really good new piece in the new  republic by alex shepard called trump's  missing phone records have a familiar  stink of criminality  and in that article  alex shepherd  discusses the analogies here to  watergate and  mentions that in terms of the amount of  missing phone data  it is more than 20 times longer in terms  of a gap in the records than what there  was in the watergate tapes i don't know  how many have recently reviewed  watergate and all of its different  elements but one of the things about  watergate was a gap in tapes which  ultimately scandalized richard nixon and  led to his resignation in 1974  and the gap in the record with these  trump phone calls is more than 20 times  bigger than the gap in that  in the watergate tapes the difference of  course is that at the time richard nixon  was president and so the entire scandal  precipitated his resignation trump is no  longer president and of course you and i  would like to think if people are  reasonable republicans would say okay  even if i liked his tax plan this is  just too much i can't vote for the guy  in 2024. unfortunately  that's not the case and not only are  there tens of millions of voters at  least still willing to vote for donald  trump still eager to vote for donald  trump in 2024  they become more emboldened by these  stories if you go and you look at  right-wing youtube right-wing twitter  right-wing tick-tock shows like real  america's voice and news max and all  these different places you see that they  are actually emboldened by these stories  saying these are part of the witch hunt  attacks meant to take down trump  unfairly  we renew our support for him  as a result of this investigation which  is really scary stuff we'll have all  these articles and more on our instagram  you can follow us there at david pakman  show we'll take a break we will talk  about that rick scott 11 point wacky  plan  after this short break

